{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An agent in the browser cannot see the internals of your library. WebMCP tools give that agent a way to read those internals during development."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerDevtoolsTools"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/devtools-webmcp"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"register-the-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register the Tools"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/devtools-webmcp"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/devtools-webmcp","lang":"sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The package has no runtime dependencies."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":2,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paste this call into your library."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp'\n\nconst stop = registerDevtoolsTools({\n  pluginId: 'tanstack.query',\n  instanceId: 'main',\n  tools: [\n    {\n      name: 'getQueryCache',\n      description: 'Return a JSON summary of the query cache.',\n      inputSchema: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          queryHash: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n      },\n      execute: (input) => summarize(client, input),\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nstop()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client"},{"type":"text","value":" are your own library code."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":3,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the tools must stay, do not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the tools must leave the page, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"names","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Names"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pluginId"},{"type":"text","value":" is required. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":" means the same thing as no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":". An empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":" is legal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The browser tool name is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pluginId.name"},{"type":"text","value":". When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":" is a non-empty string, the browser tool name is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pluginId.instanceId.name"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the sample, the browser tool name is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.query.main.getQueryCache"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A part is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pluginId"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":". When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":" is a non-empty string, that value is also a part."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each part is a non-empty string. Each part uses only ASCII letters ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"A-Z"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a-z"},{"type":"text","value":"), digits, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"."},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full tool name has 1 to 128 characters."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tool-fields","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool Fields"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"description"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":": the last part of the browser tool name."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"description"},{"type":"text","value":": the text that the agent reads."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"title"},{"type":"text","value":": an optional string."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":": an optional JSON Schema."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute"},{"type":"text","value":": the function that returns the data."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TInput"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":". This package does not read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" into TypeScript types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute"},{"type":"text","value":" receives the input and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ signal }"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal"},{"type":"text","value":" is an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The return value is data that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify"},{"type":"text","value":" can serialize. The helper sends that value to the browser with no change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The helper sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"annotations.debugging"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you set one of these hints, the helper sends that hint with the tool."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readOnlyHint"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"untrustedContentHint"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"consequentialHint"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These hints do not change "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debugging"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"development-and-production","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Development and Production"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the root import for development."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.env.NODE_ENV"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'development'"},{"type":"text","value":", the root import is the real helper. In every other environment, the root import is a no-op. An unset "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NODE_ENV"},{"type":"text","value":" is a no-op too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bundlers remove the real helper. The tool objects stay in the library bundle. The no-op does not call the browser. The no-op does not keep the tools object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the tools must stay registered in production, import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production"},{"type":"text","value":" is always the real helper. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerDevtoolsTools"},{"type":"text","value":" call stays the same. Read "},{"type":"link","href":"./production","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the production build."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"browser-lookup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser Lookup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerTool"},{"type":"text","value":" is a function on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.modelContext"},{"type":"text","value":", the helper uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.modelContext"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When that function is not on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.modelContext"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"navigator.modelContext.registerTool"},{"type":"text","value":" is a function, the helper uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"navigator.modelContext"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When neither object has that function, the call returns a cleanup function. The call does not throw. The helper writes nothing to the console on this path."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These environments take this path:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"server render"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"browser with no WebMCP"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"replace-and-remove","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace and Remove"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortController"},{"type":"text","value":" is for the whole list. The helper passes that signal to each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerTool"},{"type":"text","value":" call. The helper passes the same signal to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ signal }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup aborts that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortController"},{"type":"text","value":" and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute"},{"type":"text","value":". Then the browser removes the tools."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The call returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"},{"type":"text","value":" at once. The call does not return the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerTool"},{"type":"text","value":" promise."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A second call with the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pluginId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":" replaces the previous list. That call aborts the previous controller. Then the previous "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop"},{"type":"text","value":" function does nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A hot reload calls the helper a second time with the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pluginId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" array removes the previous tools for that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pluginId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":". The helper registers no tools on that call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The helper writes one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.error"},{"type":"text","value":" for each error. The helper does not throw. The helper logs a rejected "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerTool"},{"type":"text","value":" promise. When the helper aborts the signal, a rejection from that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerTool"},{"type":"text","value":" call writes no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.error"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pluginId"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":" is illegal, the helper registers nothing and the previous registration stays. An empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instanceId"},{"type":"text","value":" is legal."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a tool "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" is illegal, or the full name is longer than 128 characters, the helper skips that tool. Legal tools in the same list still register."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the list repeats a full name, the browser rejects the second tool. The helper logs that error, and the first tool stays registered."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If other code owns that full name, the browser rejects that tool. The helper logs the error and skips that tool."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot serialize "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":", the browser rejects that tool. The helper logs the error and continues with the other tools."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"result","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These tools do not appear in a devtools panel."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The agent can call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.query.main.getQueryCache"},{"type":"text","value":". The tool returns the value from your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize"},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"register-the-tools","text":"Register the Tools","level":2},{"id":"names","text":"Names","level":2},{"id":"tool-fields","text":"Tool Fields","level":2},{"id":"development-and-production","text":"Development and Production","level":2},{"id":"browser-lookup","text":"Browser Lookup","level":2},{"id":"replace-and-remove","text":"Replace and Remove","level":2},{"id":"errors","text":"Errors","level":2},{"id":"result","text":"Result","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nAn agent in the browser cannot see the internals of your library. WebMCP tools give that agent a way to read those internals during development.\n\nCall `registerDevtoolsTools` from `@tanstack/devtools-webmcp`.\n\n## Register the Tools\n\n1. Install `@tanstack/devtools-webmcp`.\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/devtools-webmcp\n```\n\nThe package has no runtime dependencies.\n\n2. Paste this call into your library.\n\n```ts\nimport { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp'\n\nconst stop = registerDevtoolsTools({\n  pluginId: 'tanstack.query',\n  instanceId: 'main',\n  tools: [\n    {\n      name: 'getQueryCache',\n      description: 'Return a JSON summary of the query cache.',\n      inputSchema: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          queryHash: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n      },\n      execute: (input) => summarize(client, input),\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nstop()\n```\n\n`summarize` and `client` are your own library code.\n\n3. If the tools must stay, do not call `stop()`.\n4. When the tools must leave the page, call `stop()`.\n\n## Names\n\n`pluginId` is required. `instanceId` is optional.\n\nAn empty `instanceId` means the same thing as no `instanceId`. An empty `instanceId` is legal.\n\nThe browser tool name is `pluginId.name`. When `instanceId` is a non-empty string, the browser tool name is `pluginId.instanceId.name`.\n\nIn the sample, the browser tool name is `tanstack.query.main.getQueryCache`.\n\nA part is `pluginId` or `name`. When `instanceId` is a non-empty string, that value is also a part.\n\nEach part is a non-empty string. Each part uses only ASCII letters (`A-Z` and `a-z`), digits, `_`, `-`, and `.`.\n\nThe full tool name has 1 to 128 characters.\n\n## Tool Fields\n\nA tool needs `name`, `description`, and `execute`.\n\n- `name`: the last part of the browser tool name.\n- `description`: the text that the agent reads.\n- `title`: an optional string.\n- `inputSchema`: an optional JSON Schema.\n- `execute`: the function that returns the data.\n\n`TInput` defaults to `any`. This package does not read `inputSchema` into TypeScript types.\n\n`execute` receives the input and `{ signal }`. The `signal` is an `AbortSignal`.\n\nThe return value is data that `JSON.stringify` can serialize. The helper sends that value to the browser with no change.\n\nThe helper sets `annotations.debugging` to `true`.\n\nWhen you set one of these hints, the helper sends that hint with the tool.\n\n- `readOnlyHint`\n- `untrustedContentHint`\n- `consequentialHint`\n\nThese hints do not change `debugging`.\n\n## Development and Production\n\nUse the root import for development.\n\n```ts\nimport { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp'\n```\n\nWhen `process.env.NODE_ENV` is `'development'`, the root import is the real helper. In every other environment, the root import is a no-op. An unset `NODE_ENV` is a no-op too.\n\nBundlers remove the real helper. The tool objects stay in the library bundle. The no-op does not call the browser. The no-op does not keep the tools object.\n\nIf the tools must stay registered in production, import `@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production`.\n\n```ts\nimport { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production'\n```\n\nThe import `@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production` is always the real helper. The `registerDevtoolsTools` call stays the same. Read [Production](./production) for the production build.\n\n## Browser Lookup\n\nWhen `registerTool` is a function on `document.modelContext`, the helper uses `document.modelContext`.\n\nWhen that function is not on `document.modelContext`, and `navigator.modelContext.registerTool` is a function, the helper uses `navigator.modelContext`.\n\nWhen neither object has that function, the call returns a cleanup function. The call does not throw. The helper writes nothing to the console on this path.\n\nThese environments take this path:\n\n- server render\n- Node\n- browser with no WebMCP\n\n## Replace and Remove\n\nOne `AbortController` is for the whole list. The helper passes that signal to each `registerTool` call. The helper passes the same signal to `execute` as `{ signal }`.\n\nCleanup aborts that `AbortController` and the `signal` in `execute`. Then the browser removes the tools.\n\nThe call returns `stop` at once. The call does not return the `registerTool` promise.\n\nA second call with the same `pluginId` and `instanceId` replaces the previous list. That call aborts the previous controller. Then the previous `stop` function does nothing.\n\nA hot reload calls the helper a second time with the same `pluginId` and `instanceId`.\n\nAn empty `tools` array removes the previous tools for that `pluginId` and `instanceId`. The helper registers no tools on that call.\n\n## Errors\n\nThe helper writes one `console.error` for each error. The helper does not throw. The helper logs a rejected `registerTool` promise. When the helper aborts the signal, a rejection from that `registerTool` call writes no `console.error`.\n\n- If `pluginId` or `instanceId` is illegal, the helper registers nothing and the previous registration stays. An empty `instanceId` is legal.\n- If a tool `name` is illegal, or the full name is longer than 128 characters, the helper skips that tool. Legal tools in the same list still register.\n- If the list repeats a full name, the browser rejects the second tool. The helper logs that error, and the first tool stays registered.\n- If other code owns that full name, the browser rejects that tool. The helper logs the error and skips that tool.\n- If `JSON.stringify` cannot serialize `inputSchema`, the browser rejects that tool. The helper logs the error and continues with the other tools.\n\n## Result\n\nThese tools do not appear in a devtools panel.\n\nThe agent can call `tanstack.query.main.getQueryCache`. The tool returns the value from your `summarize` function.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: WebMCP Tools\nid: webmcp-tools\n---\n\nAn agent in the browser cannot see the internals of your library. WebMCP tools give that agent a way to read those internals during development.\n\nCall `registerDevtoolsTools` from `@tanstack/devtools-webmcp`.\n\n## Register the Tools\n\n1. Install `@tanstack/devtools-webmcp`.\n\n```sh\nnpm install @tanstack/devtools-webmcp\n```\n\nThe package has no runtime dependencies.\n\n2. Paste this call into your library.\n\n```ts\nimport { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp'\n\nconst stop = registerDevtoolsTools({\n  pluginId: 'tanstack.query',\n  instanceId: 'main',\n  tools: [\n    {\n      name: 'getQueryCache',\n      description: 'Return a JSON summary of the query cache.',\n      inputSchema: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          queryHash: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n      },\n      execute: (input) => summarize(client, input),\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nstop()\n```\n\n`summarize` and `client` are your own library code.\n\n3. If the tools must stay, do not call `stop()`.\n4. When the tools must leave the page, call `stop()`.\n\n## Names\n\n`pluginId` is required. `instanceId` is optional.\n\nAn empty `instanceId` means the same thing as no `instanceId`. An empty `instanceId` is legal.\n\nThe browser tool name is `pluginId.name`. When `instanceId` is a non-empty string, the browser tool name is `pluginId.instanceId.name`.\n\nIn the sample, the browser tool name is `tanstack.query.main.getQueryCache`.\n\nA part is `pluginId` or `name`. When `instanceId` is a non-empty string, that value is also a part.\n\nEach part is a non-empty string. Each part uses only ASCII letters (`A-Z` and `a-z`), digits, `_`, `-`, and `.`.\n\nThe full tool name has 1 to 128 characters.\n\n## Tool Fields\n\nA tool needs `name`, `description`, and `execute`.\n\n- `name`: the last part of the browser tool name.\n- `description`: the text that the agent reads.\n- `title`: an optional string.\n- `inputSchema`: an optional JSON Schema.\n- `execute`: the function that returns the data.\n\n`TInput` defaults to `any`. This package does not read `inputSchema` into TypeScript types.\n\n`execute` receives the input and `{ signal }`. The `signal` is an `AbortSignal`.\n\nThe return value is data that `JSON.stringify` can serialize. The helper sends that value to the browser with no change.\n\nThe helper sets `annotations.debugging` to `true`.\n\nWhen you set one of these hints, the helper sends that hint with the tool.\n\n- `readOnlyHint`\n- `untrustedContentHint`\n- `consequentialHint`\n\nThese hints do not change `debugging`.\n\n## Development and Production\n\nUse the root import for development.\n\n```ts\nimport { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp'\n```\n\nWhen `process.env.NODE_ENV` is `'development'`, the root import is the real helper. In every other environment, the root import is a no-op. An unset `NODE_ENV` is a no-op too.\n\nBundlers remove the real helper. The tool objects stay in the library bundle. The no-op does not call the browser. The no-op does not keep the tools object.\n\nIf the tools must stay registered in production, import `@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production`.\n\n```ts\nimport { registerDevtoolsTools } from '@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production'\n```\n\nThe import `@tanstack/devtools-webmcp/production` is always the real helper. The `registerDevtoolsTools` call stays the same. Read [Production](./production) for the production build.\n\n## Browser Lookup\n\nWhen `registerTool` is a function on `document.modelContext`, the helper uses `document.modelContext`.\n\nWhen that function is not on `document.modelContext`, and `navigator.modelContext.registerTool` is a function, the helper uses `navigator.modelContext`.\n\nWhen neither object has that function, the call returns a cleanup function. The call does not throw. The helper writes nothing to the console on this path.\n\nThese environments take this path:\n\n- server render\n- Node\n- browser with no WebMCP\n\n## Replace and Remove\n\nOne `AbortController` is for the whole list. The helper passes that signal to each `registerTool` call. The helper passes the same signal to `execute` as `{ signal }`.\n\nCleanup aborts that `AbortController` and the `signal` in `execute`. Then the browser removes the tools.\n\nThe call returns `stop` at once. The call does not return the `registerTool` promise.\n\nA second call with the same `pluginId` and `instanceId` replaces the previous list. That call aborts the previous controller. Then the previous `stop` function does nothing.\n\nA hot reload calls the helper a second time with the same `pluginId` and `instanceId`.\n\nAn empty `tools` array removes the previous tools for that `pluginId` and `instanceId`. The helper registers no tools on that call.\n\n## Errors\n\nThe helper writes one `console.error` for each error. The helper does not throw. The helper logs a rejected `registerTool` promise. When the helper aborts the signal, a rejection from that `registerTool` call writes no `console.error`.\n\n- If `pluginId` or `instanceId` is illegal, the helper registers nothing and the previous registration stays. An empty `instanceId` is legal.\n- If a tool `name` is illegal, or the full name is longer than 128 characters, the helper skips that tool. Legal tools in the same list still register.\n- If the list repeats a full name, the browser rejects the second tool. The helper logs that error, and the first tool stays registered.\n- If other code owns that full name, the browser rejects that tool. The helper logs the error and skips that tool.\n- If `JSON.stringify` cannot serialize `inputSchema`, the browser rejects that tool. The helper logs the error and continues with the other tools.\n\n## Result\n\nThese tools do not appear in a devtools panel.\n\nThe agent can call `tanstack.query.main.getQueryCache`. The tool returns the value from your `summarize` function.\n"}
